masscan
Usage: masscan -pPORTS RANGE --rate N [-oL FILE]

An internet-scale port scanner: stateless, so it finds open ports across huge
ranges very fast -- then you point nmap at only the hosts that answered. It is
loud by nature; the rate controls how loud.

	-p1-65535     the ports to probe (a range or list)
	--rate N      packets per second -- higher is faster and louder
	-oL FILE      write the open ports to a file

Only against networks you own or are authorised to test. In this school the
target is always `127.0.0.1`.

See also: nmap, tcpdump
